<title>MEXICO: MEXICO'S DURANGO STATE SEES 1997 GOLD OUTPUT UP.</title>
<headline>MEXICO'S DURANGO STATE SEES 1997 GOLD OUTPUT UP.</headline>
<dateline>GUADALAJARA, Mexico 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's northwestern state of Durango estimates its gold output this year will rise 10.72 percent over that produced in 1996, according to a document obtained by Reuters on Wednesday.</p>
<p>According to statistics that will be presented in September in the state government's annual report, 1997 output of the previous metal will be 5,184 kg, against 4,682 kg in 1996.</p>
<p>Gold production in Durango was 1,844 kg and rose to 3,950 kg in 1995. Durango is the second gold-producing state in Mexico.</p>
<p>Silver output in the state is seen climbing to 383,253 tonnes against the 376,673 tonnes produced in 1996, the document predicted.</p>
<p>((--Monica Ballesca, Guadalajara bureau +523 817-0397))</p>
